.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt O2I_SCT_LIST 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm o2i_SCT_LIST ,
.Nm i2o_SCT_LIST ,
.Nm o2i_SCT ,
.Nm i2o_SCT
.Nd decode and encode Signed Certificate Timestamp lists in TLS wire format
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In openssl/ct.h
.Bd -literal
 STACK_OF(SCT) *o2i_SCT_LIST(STACK_OF(SCT) **a, const unsigned char **pp,
                             size_t len);
 int i2o_SCT_LIST(const STACK_OF(SCT) *a, unsigned char **pp);
 SCT *o2i_SCT(SCT **psct, const unsigned char **in, size_t len);
 int i2o_SCT(const SCT *sct, unsigned char **out);
.Ed
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The SCT_LIST and SCT functions are very similar to the i2d and d2i
family of functions, except that they convert to and from TLS wire
format, as described in RFC 6962. See
.Xr d2i_SCT_LIST 3
for more information about how the parameters are treated and the return
values.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
All of the functions have return values consistent with those stated for
.Xr d2i_SCT_LIST 3
and
.Xr i2d_SCT_LIST 3 .
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ct 7 ,
.Xr d2i_SCT_LIST 3 ,
.Xr i2d_SCT_LIST 3
.Sh HISTORY
These functions were added in OpenSSL 1.1.0.
